                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The video and screenshots are impressive and I love magical story-driven action/adventure games. So although I read about the game being (very) short for the price they're asking, I still couldn't resist.  Here are my thoughts:\n\nPRO\n\n-  I love the mysterious and magical story and the overall cinematic feel of the game\n-  The bow and shield look and feel really awesome!  \n-  fantastic voice-acting, sounds and perfect music \n-  excellent game mechanics\n\nCON\n\n- it's curently way too expensive for the content.  The DEV team is talking about episodes, but it's unclear whether they will be added for free (and when they will be added). This game is not EA so more clarity about upcoming content (content that continues the story) would be welcome. The game is short and, at one point, it's even artifically extended by a long wave of similar enemies\n\n- a potentially very beautiful environment IF I wouldn't be seeing blurry, jaggy graphics.  There's no supersampling option in the game-menu(?!) and using supersampling from the Advanced Settings add-on in SteamVR didn't change anything.  I would say the default setting now is something like low or medium, while I wanted to play on high or epic.  Bummer :(  This can be quite easily fixed if the DEV team would allow for an in-game SS option.  I've seen this so many tims with UE4 games :  when there's no in-game SS, the game is way too blurry, especially for GTX 1070 and 1080 owners who are used to upscaling their games significantly.\n\n-  gameplay is a mixture of simple but logical (and magical) puzzles (wheel turning to bounce light beams) and shooting with a bow. No free movement, only teleport to fix points.  \n\n- the in-game menu looks like it's thrown into the game afterwards and rather quickly.  It looks sloppy and ugly and there's little to nothing that can be changed or customized\n\nCONCLUSIONS\n\n- if your budget is limited, don't buy it\n- if you have a problem with stationary/wave-shooting type of games, don't buy it\n- if you don't like short games, don't buy it\n\nBUT\n\n- if you can spare 11 EUR and you love short but magical story-driven games with sweet graphics (after they add supersampling), you might like it....\n\nBottomline :  I can't recommended in the current state, for the price they're asking now.... \n@DEV-team : please add another episode or lower the price to approx. 5 EUR and add supersampling or high/epic graphics!",
